{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589589503,"sessionID":"ses_e2a20a4d7ffeIt6OmrD13sAn8e","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5dffe16001Z7NUKf2C52KGdA","sessionID":"ses_e2a20a4d7ffeIt6OmrD13sAn8e","messageID":"msg_1d5dfe0bb001mr38nKXPW2x5ko","type":"tool","id":"call_36dc379d6e8044cea61fbbdd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/references/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/references/README.md, lines 1-57\n1: ---\n2: title: create-readme Reference Map\n3: description: Overflow-only route map for README authoring, grouped into readme/ single-concern references.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"readme reference map\"\n6:   - \"readme creation standards\"\n7:   - \"create-readme references\"\n8: importance_tier: normal\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 1.1.0.7\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # create-readme Reference Map\n14: \n15: Overflow route map for the `create-readme` packet. The complete authoring workflows live in [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md); this set holds only the deep detail those workflows point to.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: `SKILL.md` is primary and self-sufficient: it carries the full README authoring workflow (Section 4) and the general and code-folder output shapes (Sections 5 and 6). Open a file below only when a task needs the extra depth, and load the single file that matches the concern rather than a large monolith.\n22: \n23: The overflow sits in one group: `readme/` holds README type, voice, writing-pattern and quality detail.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n28: \n29: Load the file that matches the current task.\n30: \n31: | Concern | Reference | Load When |\n32: | --- | --- | --- |\n33: | **README types and voice**: the five README types, progressive-disclosure stages and two-tier voice with worked examples | [readme/types-and-voice.md](readme/types-and-voice.md) | Deciding which README type to write, or how narrative and reference voice should split inside one file |\n34: | **README writing patterns**: per-section writing tips, heading hierarchy, analogy patterns, recommended table patterns, code-block and placeholder conventions | [readme/writing-patterns.md](readme/writing-patterns.md) | Drafting individual README sections, or reaching for a proven table or formatting pattern |\n35: | **README quality and checklist**, DQI weighting, per-section quality checks and the full pre-publish checklist | [readme/quality-and-checklist.md](readme/quality-and-checklist.md) | Reviewing a drafted README before delivery |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. RELATED RESOURCES\n40: \n41: ### Overflow Subfolder\n42: - [readme/types-and-voice.md](readme/types-and-voice.md) - README types, progressive disclosure and two-tier voice\n43: - [readme/writing-patterns.md](readme/writing-patterns.md) - Section writing tips and formatting patterns\n44: - [readme/quality-and-checklist.md](readme/quality-and-checklist.md) - README quality criteria and pre-publish checklist\n45: \n46: ### Templates\n47: - [readme-template.md](../assets/readme-template.md) - Fillable scaffold for project, skill, feature and component READMEs\n48: - [readme-code-template.md](../assets/readme-code-template.md) - Code-folder README scaffold with diagram examples\n49: \n50: ### Shared Standards\n51: - [core-standards.md](../../shared/references/core-standards.md) - Document formatting rules\n52: - [hvr-rules.md](../../sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md) - Human Voice Rules\n53: - [validation.md](../../shared/references/validation.md) - Quality scoring (DQI)\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: *End of create-readme reference map: depth lives in the `readme/` group.*","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/references/README.md, lines 1-57\n1: ---\n2: title: create-readme Reference Map\n3: description: Overflow-only route map for README authoring, grouped into readme/ single-concern references.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"readme reference map\"\n6:   - \"readme creation standards\"\n7:   - \"create-readme references\"\n8: importance_tier: normal\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 1.1.0.7\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # create-readme Reference Map\n14: \n15: Overflow route map for the `create-readme` packet. The complete authoring workflows live in [`../SKILL.md`](../SKILL.md); this set holds only the deep detail those workflows point to.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n20: \n21: `SKILL.md` is primary and self-sufficient: it carries the full README authoring workflow (Section 4) and the general and code-folder output shapes (Sections 5 and 6). Open a file below only when a task needs the extra depth, and load the single file that matches the concern rather than a large monolith.\n22: \n23: The overflow sits in one group: `readme/` holds README type, voice, writing-pattern and quality detail.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ## 2. REFERENCE MAP\n28: \n29: Load the file that matches the current task.\n30: \n31: | Concern | Reference | Load When |\n32: | --- | --- | --- |\n33: | **README types and voice**: the five README types, progressive-disclosure stages and two-tier voice with worked examples | [readme/types-and-voice.md](readme/types-and-voice.md) | Deciding which README type to write, or how narrative and reference voice should split inside one file |\n34: | **README writing patterns**: per-section writing tips, heading hierarchy, analogy patterns, recommended table patterns, code-block and placeholder conventions | [readme/writing-patterns.md](readme/writing-patterns.md) | Drafting individual README sections, or reaching for a proven table or formatting pattern |\n35: | **README quality and checklist**, DQI weighting, per-section quality checks and the full pre-publish checklist | [readme/quality-and-checklist.md](readme/quality-and-checklist.md) | Reviewing a drafted README before delivery |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. RELATED RESOURCES\n40: \n41: ### Overflow Subfolder\n42: - [readme/types-and-voice.md](readme/types-and-voice.md) - README types, progressive disclosure and two-tier voice\n43: - [readme/writing-patterns.md](readme/writing-patterns.md) - Section writing tips and formatting patterns\n44: - [readme/quality-and-checklist.md](readme/quality-and-checklist.md) - README quality criteria and pre-publish checklist\n45: \n46: ### Templates\n47: - [readme-template.md](../assets/readme-template.md) - Fillable scaffold for project, skill, feature and component READMEs\n48: - [readme-code-template.md](../assets/readme-code-template.md) - Code-folder README scaffold with diagram examples\n49: \n50: ### Shared Standards\n51: - [core-standards.md](../../shared/references/core-standards.md) - Document formatting rules\n52: - [hvr-rules.md](../../sk-create-with-human-voice/references/hvr-rules.md) - Human Voice Rules\n53: - [validation.md](../../shared/references/validation.md) - Quality scoring (DQI)\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: *End of create-readme reference map: depth lives in the `readme/` group.*"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/references/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589589014,"end":1794589589503}}}}
